Argyle is a tall man in [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] who smells of frankincense and myrrh, wears armor, and carries a shield. He is a trained healer, and is a contact of [[Org/The Scale/People/Dame Quay|Dame Quay]] in [[Org/The Scale/index|the Scale]]. He talks like an officer of the Scale, asks to be called Dr. Argyle, FFCS, apprentice timekeeper, and holds that hiding is a form of lying.

He was killed in the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]], and his soul did not return with the others; the Party dreamed of it chained between a light pulling up and a dark pulling down.

Argyle came back from the dead. He says the [[Divinity/Outer Gods/Judge of Ages|Judge]] ripped him from perdition and set him back in the same body, a little taller and with different eyes, his raiment twice the size it had been. He is closer to the Judge now and carries less of another influence, which he will not name. Only part of him returned: he calls the rest a philosophical perdition. He is looking for the other half, which he understands went voidward, and says the halves were bonded and are meant to be bonded. [[Org/The Scale/People/Dame Quay|Dame Quay]] expects him to find that half on the coming [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]], and says the old binding ritual will not serve because the two separated on bad terms. The other half is also part of the Judge, he does not mean to kill it, and anyone who sees another Argyle should tell him at once, since it is likely a demon wearing his face.

The [[People/Sharp the Cunning Man|Cunning Man]] checked him and found no demon or devil in him, and he rejoined the others at the [[Sin and Tonic]]. He now gives free medicine to people who cannot pay, working as a back-alley surgeon, and keeps his money in small jewels rather than trust the money system.
